/T (On the ground of fraud, a Policy of Life Insurance may be called in question at any time within 3 years from the date of issuance of Policy or the date of commencement of risk or the date of Revival of  Policy or the date of rider to the Policy, whichever is later. For this, the insurer shall have to communicate in writing to the Insured or legal representative or nominee or assignees of Insured, as applicable, mentioning the ground and materials on which such decision is based. For full texts of Section 38, Section 39, Section 41 and Section 45, please refer to the Insurance Act, 1938 \(as amended from time to time\). )
